  "simulator": {
    "adapter": "comb-over",
    "netlist": ".title 10 dB coupled-line coupler on JLC RO4350B 0.508 mm, from physical dimensions (5 GHz)\n# The section is given by strip width W and gap S; Z0e/Z0o, the even/odd effective permittivities\n# and the per-mode losses come from the microstrip models (manual §4.6) for the .substrate below.\n# W and S are tunable, so the optimiser can adjust the actual copper dimensions.\n.freq 1G 9G 801\n.ref 5G\n.substrate jlc-ro4350b-0.508\n.param w = 0.8831mm tune 0.5mm 1.3mm\n.param s = 0.1025mm tune 0.1mm 0.4mm      # 0.1 mm is JLC's minimum space\nport in    # 1\nport thru  # 2\nport cpl   # 3\nport iso   # 4\ncline K geom=msl W=w S=s\n  len 90deg                 # at .ref, mean modal velocity\n  A in   cpl\n  B thru iso\nend\n.goal db(S31) = -10 4.5G 5.5G\n.goal db(S11) < -25 4G 6G\n.plot ylim=-50,0 db(S11) db(S21) db(S31) db(S41)\n.plot title=Directivity_(dB) db(S31/S41)\n.layout coupler K\n",
    "factors": {
      "etch": {
        "etch": true
      },
      "er": {
        "substrate": "er"
      }
    },
    "metrics": {
      "coupling": "-db(S31) @ 5G",
      "directivity": "db(S31/S41) @ 5G"
    }
  },
  "history": [],
  "description": "Worked example for the comb-over adapter (#21): the 10 dB coupled-line coupler of comb-over examples/coupler-10dB-ro4350b.cir (JLC RO4350B 0.508 mm, 5 GHz). Factors: etch bias per edge (µm; positive narrows the strips and widens the gap), sd 8 µm — an assumed value, not a JLCPCB figure; substrate εr, sd 0.025 (Rogers quotes ±0.05 on Dk). Specs: coupling 10 ± 0.5 dB and directivity ≥ 12 dB at 5 GHz. (The issue asked for directivity > 15 dB; this design has 13.2 dB nominal, so 15 dB would give zero yield.) A cubic etch term (coupling ~ quadratic + I(etch^3)) cuts the surrogate error by about 3×."
}
